"source": [
"## What to notice\n",
"- fp16/bf16/TF32 crush fp32 - that is the **tensor cores**. On CPU (M0) you had one ceiling; on GPU you have several, one per precision.\n",
"- The GPU's peak memory bandwidth (hundreds of GB/s) dwarfs a CPU's (~10 GB/s from M0) - yet pooling is *still* memory-bound. Arithmetic intensity, not raw FLOPS,\n",
"decides the ceiling. That idea is hardware-independent.\n",
"- Compare your numbers to M0/M1 (CPU): the GPU is ~10-100x on compute-bound ops, but far less on memory-bound ones.\n",
"\n",
